+# Final review inv-2, cluster 23 (evidence-hg-lnw-9)
+
+Source: base 60e287aadd08af10779df39e625200f28d4b7fa3, head 985d1eb6faaa2e92e4e01f430f0f2c07618bf6ad (both verified with `git rev-parse --verify`; bind-review-source succeeded). Caller checkout observed clean at head.
+Inputs: the five `evidence/hg-lnw.9/*.log` files (slices 000132-000136), digest.md, the hg-lnw design doc (it has a Requirement baseline section).
+
+## What the cluster is
+
+Five text logs from task hg-lnw.9 (commit 8c32c83). No production code, no test code. The cluster cannot deliver or fail a baseline row by itself. Any row that runs through the code these logs exercise belongs to the seam reviewer.
+
+## What the logs show
+
+- tier3-final-rebased.log: full tier-3 run on the rebased task tip. 28 binaries pass, including e2e_private_herdr 42/42 and herdr_client 7/7. One failure, test_isolation `test_sources_spawn_only_through_isolated_helpers`, on `tests/threads_real.rs:50` (rule R1, raw `std::process::Command::new`). Exit 101.
+- base-057ad4d-isolation-lint.log: the same R1 hit at the base commit, so the lint failure predates hg-lnw.9. Commit 4327d3f (hg-lnw.22) is an ancestor of the reviewed head and edits tests/threads_real.rs and tests/support/private_herdr.rs. At head, line 50 of threads_real.rs calls `support::private_herdr::private_command`. The hit is gone from the source.
+- tier3-run2-summary.log: an earlier run with 3 failures: late_rebind, undo_restored_agent_that_exits_is_relaunched_live and private_process_info_is_shell. The final rebased log passes all three. That means two e2e tests and one client test changed result between runs with no source change recorded in this cluster. They are timing-sensitive.
+- base-private_process_info_is_shell.log: 5 passes and 1 failure in 6 runs at the base commit. The flake is not caused by hg-lnw.9. The failure message in run2 is `foreground argv: []`, a race reading the foreground process.
+- late-rebind-pinned-order.log: a single pass of `late_rebind_binds_the_fresh_agent_at_its_next_prompt` (232 s). It shows the intended order: the seat reads `unresolved` and the check-in is refused with TargetUnresolved and the rebind remedy; after the graph rebind the seat reads `resolved`; the next prompt hook returns the normal check-in; the seat becomes `active: true, available`. The run needed pinned ordering because the test failed in 2 of 5 runs without it (progress.md, Minor entry for hg-lnw.9).
+
+## Observations on the evidence
+
+- The final rebased log is a failing run (exit 101). Its one failure is explained and has a later fix (hg-lnw.22). I did not re-run tier 3 at head. The full tier-3 run takes about 20 minutes and spends the SSD and pid budget, and this cluster does not change code.
+- The logs embed the task worktree path (`.worktrees/...--task-hg-lnw.9`), which has since been removed. That is only cosmetic.
+- The late-rebind evidence is the pinned-order single run. A flake of 2 in 5 is recorded as a minor in the ledger, but I found no follow-up bead for it in the files I read.
+
+## Verdict
+
+ready
+
